---
import DefaultLayout from '@layouts/DefaultLayout.astro'
import ContentMedia from '@components/ContentMedia.astro'
import Hero from '@components/Hero.astro'
import Feature from '@components/Feature.astro'
import FeaturedPosts from '@components/FeaturedPosts.astro'
import FeaturedProjects from '@components/FeaturedProjects.astro'
import { Link, Heading } from 'accessible-astro-components'
---

<DefaultLayout title="Alyson Thomas of Premier Plus Realty" useTitleTemplate={false}>
  <Hero class="theme__emphasis"/>

  <section class="py-16 theme__alternate">
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-14"> 
      <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-amber-100 text-amber-900 border border-amber-300 mb-3">
        Highlands County Seller Advantage
      </span> 
      <Heading level="h2">Why Sellers Choose Alyson</Heading>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-xl">
        Selling a home in Sebring requires nuanced local market insight, disciplined pricing, and aggressive buyer outreach. Here is how Alyson delivers top-dollar results for Highlands County homeowners.
      </p> 
    </div>
    <div class="container grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <Feature icon="lucide:chart-no-axes-combined" title="Expert Pricing Strategy" level="h3">
        Alyson performs a Comparative Market Analysis (CMA) analyzing recent verified sales in your specific area to position your home at peak market value without risking costly days on market.
      </Feature>
      <Feature icon="lucide:globe-check" title="Maximum Market Exposure" level="h3">
        Every listing receives comprehensive marketing designed to captivate active buyers across Florida and out-of-state relocations. 
      </Feature>
      <Feature icon="lucide:heart-handshake" title="Personal Attention" level="h3">
        When you list with Alyson, you work directly with her from the initial pre-listing consultation to closing day. You receive consistent updates every step of the journey.
      </Feature>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 grid place-content-center">
      <Link
            href="https://github.com/incluud/accessible-astro-starter"
            isButton
            type="secondary"
            animateOnHover
            animationType="boop"
          >
            Get Your Free Home Valuation
          </Link>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ContentMedia imgSrc="social-preview-image.png">
    <Heading level="h2">Sebring, FL</Heading>
    <p class="text-2xl">
      Known as "The City on the Circle," Sebring combines peaceful Florida Heartland charm, over 80 freshwater lakes, championship golf courses, and an exceptionally accessible cost of living. Whether you are seeking a premier 55+ active adult community, a fairway estate, or a private lakefront sanctuary, Alyson Thomas provides the local market insight you need.</p>
    <p>One reason for purchasing a home in Sebring is affordability. The single-family home price in Sebring gives buyers significantly more square footage, larger lot sizes, and modern community amenities for their investment.
    </p>
  </ContentMedia>
  <ContentMedia imgSrc="social-preview-image.png" reverseImg={true}>
    <Heading level="h2">Avon Park, FL</Heading>
    <p class="text-2xl">
      Avon Park is Highlands County’s oldest incorporated municipality, and its median home prices sit approximately 10% to 15% below neighboring Sebring. northern location shaves 15 to 20 minutes off the commute to Winter Haven, Lakeland, and the Greater Orlando metroplex.
    </p>
  </ContentMedia>
<ContentMedia imgSrc="social-preview-image.png">
    <Heading level="h2">Lake Placid, FL</Heading>
    <p class="text-2xl">
       Lake Placid is celebrated nationally as both Florida's "Town of Murals" and the "Caladium Capital of the World.  Lake Placid has a high concentration of second homes and seasonal residences. Buyers prioritize low-maintenance landscaping, hurricane shutters, screened lanais, and garage space for golf carts and boat trailers.
    </p>
  </ContentMedia>
  <FeaturedPosts />
  <FeaturedProjects />
</DefaultLayout>
